270
00:22:05,925 --> 00:22:06,385
[SPEAKER_03]: Apparently,

271
00:22:08,336 --> 00:22:11,918
[SPEAKER_03]: The owner confirmed that they could do this without getting a variance.

272
00:22:12,398 --> 00:22:20,842
[SPEAKER_03]: So we did try to push them to go a little higher, but that would have put them into variance territory.

273
00:22:20,922 --> 00:22:25,264
[SPEAKER_03]: So they declined to entertain that.

274
00:22:26,584 --> 00:22:29,445
[SPEAKER_03]: So this would be the scheme we're voting on.

275
00:22:32,176 --> 00:22:34,238
[SPEAKER_03]: whether to lift the demo delay.

276
00:22:34,558 --> 00:22:38,581
[SPEAKER_03]: And I feel like it has come a long way since the original one.

277
00:22:39,582 --> 00:22:41,523
[SPEAKER_03]: It's more in character.

278
00:22:41,543 --> 00:22:44,726
[SPEAKER_03]: I had a few comments.

279
00:22:44,806 --> 00:22:47,168
[SPEAKER_03]: There weren't any quarterboards on this.

280
00:22:47,308 --> 00:22:50,370
[SPEAKER_03]: And I don't know if that's just a drafting error or what.

281
00:22:50,991 --> 00:22:54,874
[SPEAKER_03]: And there wasn't really any trim around the

282
00:22:55,623 --> 00:22:58,185
[SPEAKER_03]: you know, doors and stuff, just a J bead.

283
00:22:58,265 --> 00:23:01,988
[SPEAKER_03]: So they seem like they would be willing to entertain that.

284
00:23:04,189 --> 00:23:06,411
[SPEAKER_03]: I would like to hear from the owners on that.

285
00:23:09,313 --> 00:23:12,976
[SPEAKER_03]: And I had some comments about the garage doors.

286
00:23:14,997 --> 00:23:18,620
[SPEAKER_03]: Like that a little bit more traditional looking garage doors, but

287
00:23:20,302 --> 00:23:28,246
[SPEAKER_03]: They said based upon availability, because there are a lot of supply chain issues, the choices aren't quite what they were.

288
00:23:28,406 --> 00:23:32,989
[SPEAKER_03]: So they said they would entertain that.

289
00:23:33,409 --> 00:23:35,390
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you kind of revisit the height?

290
00:23:35,410 --> 00:23:42,654
[SPEAKER_01]: Because I'd like to know, what was the reasoning behind raising the height?

291
00:23:44,273 --> 00:23:49,136
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, we were just trying to get the roof shape to look more like a carriage house.

292
00:23:49,856 --> 00:23:55,219
[SPEAKER_03]: So if we go back to where we were, we just had this kind of, you know, that was the side view.

293
00:23:56,720 --> 00:23:57,681
[SPEAKER_03]: And it really doesn't.

294
00:23:59,042 --> 00:24:04,325
[SPEAKER_03]: It just looks like a very basic, you know, low slope shed roof.

295
00:24:04,405 --> 00:24:06,026
[SPEAKER_03]: So we were trying to kind of

296
00:24:09,265 --> 00:24:13,689
[SPEAKER_03]: push the designer to get something that was a little bit more in character.

297
00:24:15,430 --> 00:24:21,155
[SPEAKER_03]: We met with them at the property and we produced a sketch there on the spot.

298
00:24:22,736 --> 00:24:24,778
[SPEAKER_03]: They did take it to heart.

299
00:24:24,958 --> 00:24:26,940
[SPEAKER_03]: They came up with this.

300
00:24:28,541 --> 00:24:36,408
[SPEAKER_03]: There was some back and forth with the building department about what the allowable height is.

301
00:24:37,582 --> 00:24:40,224
[SPEAKER_03]: and there was this number of 15 feet.

302
00:24:40,244 --> 00:24:43,527
[SPEAKER_03]: It's not the right number, Ryan?

303
00:24:44,387 --> 00:24:44,828
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

304
00:24:45,328 --> 00:24:56,637
[SPEAKER_03]: And it was a question of, was the 15 feet to the peak of the roof or as in many cities to the midpoint of the highest roof plane?

305
00:24:57,898 --> 00:25:06,324
[SPEAKER_03]: And so we did an exchange of emails with Dennis McDonald at the building department.

306
00:25:08,868 --> 00:25:13,932
[SPEAKER_03]: I think he finally agreed that it was to the midpoint of the highest roof.

307
00:25:13,952 --> 00:25:23,159
[SPEAKER_03]: So that allowed them to make a little bit higher roof and still meet the zoning.

308
00:25:24,780 --> 00:25:26,681
[SPEAKER_01]: I'd like to see options for the doors.

309
00:25:26,781 --> 00:25:28,182
[SPEAKER_01]: I think the doors are critical.

310
00:25:28,943 --> 00:25:29,603
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, I would too.

311
00:25:29,623 --> 00:25:31,505
[SPEAKER_01]: Do we have pictures of the proposed doors?

312
00:25:32,166 --> 00:25:36,908
[SPEAKER_03]: This is what they agreed to, you know, we don't we don't have that yet.

313
00:25:38,188 --> 00:25:39,449
[SPEAKER_03]: You know.

314
00:25:41,910 --> 00:25:44,050
[SPEAKER_01]: This is one door or two doors.

315
00:25:44,070 --> 00:25:45,211
[SPEAKER_03]: I believe it's one.

316
00:25:46,405 --> 00:25:49,466
[SPEAKER_03]: but I would like the owner to speak to that.

317
00:25:50,926 --> 00:25:54,747
[SPEAKER_03]: So if you want, I can show you the sketch that I produced.

318
00:25:55,467 --> 00:25:57,308
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, I think that would be helpful.

319
00:25:57,588 --> 00:26:02,729
[SPEAKER_03]: Okay, so the one I produced was just an overlay.

320
00:26:02,769 --> 00:26:10,831
[SPEAKER_03]: So we raised everything up by two feet, and then I was looking at a kind of more of a traditional breakdown of the doors.

321
00:26:12,211 --> 00:26:15,092
[SPEAKER_03]: This could be a single door, but looking like two doors,

322
00:26:16,152 --> 00:26:21,454
[SPEAKER_03]: I added the trim around the door and the window, added the corner boards.

323
00:26:21,755 --> 00:26:27,077
[SPEAKER_03]: That was basically it, just raising this up two feet to get what I thought was a better proportion.

324
00:26:27,097 --> 00:26:31,539
[SPEAKER_03]: But donor said that that would push them into variance territory.

325
00:26:31,619 --> 00:26:40,283
[SPEAKER_03]: So I'm not sure that that's totally necessary for them to go for a variance.

326
00:26:42,045 --> 00:26:42,365
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

327
00:26:42,705 --> 00:26:47,987
[SPEAKER_03]: You know, I don't want to, I wouldn't want to make them go through that process.

328
00:26:48,808 --> 00:26:53,329
[SPEAKER_01]: Just for, I think the doors are much more critical than the height.

329
00:26:53,769 --> 00:26:54,049
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

330
00:26:54,570 --> 00:26:57,811
[SPEAKER_03]: So I don't know how you guys want to leave it.

331
00:26:57,931 --> 00:27:05,354
[SPEAKER_03]: You know, this, this is, this is what they were willing to, you know, give.

332
00:27:07,054 --> 00:27:11,556
[SPEAKER_03]: And so, you know, I, that's where we are at right now.

333
00:27:13,907 --> 00:27:20,911
[SPEAKER_02]: Jen just want to call your attention that in the chat, the finder has said they're fine with updating the trim and it's one door.

334
00:27:20,931 --> 00:27:22,432
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay.

335
00:27:22,512 --> 00:27:22,752
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

336
00:27:23,273 --> 00:27:23,613
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

337
00:27:23,893 --> 00:27:24,093
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

338
00:27:24,173 --> 00:27:35,920
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, personally, I think the doors need work and I'd like to see examples of the actual doors that will be purchased and put on before, before I'm ready to release this.

339
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:38,881
[SPEAKER_01]: If it comes down to a tie and I have to vote.

340
00:27:40,762 --> 00:27:40,923
[SPEAKER_08]: Yep.

341
00:27:42,252 --> 00:27:46,334
[SPEAKER_01]: But I mean, certainly, you know, I'm not trying to hog the conversation here.

342
00:27:46,355 --> 00:27:49,436
[SPEAKER_01]: I'd love to hear from the other commissioners, their thoughts.

343
00:27:50,297 --> 00:27:53,079
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, that's kind of my summary of the process.

344
00:27:53,139 --> 00:27:55,000
[SPEAKER_03]: I mean, we did meet with them.

345
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:57,241
[SPEAKER_03]: We went over there and met with them.

346
00:27:57,261 --> 00:28:01,864
[SPEAKER_03]: I was gone for a long, most of August.

347
00:28:01,904 --> 00:28:05,786
[SPEAKER_03]: So there wasn't much communication during that time.

348
00:28:05,846 --> 00:28:08,608
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't know if Ryan, you had any further communications with them.

349
00:28:12,268 --> 00:28:14,810
[SPEAKER_04]: No, I think the changes are not crazy here.

350
00:28:14,890 --> 00:28:17,372
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm fine with the massing now that I look at it in depth.

351
00:28:17,472 --> 00:28:22,517
[SPEAKER_04]: I agree that I don't think it's worth it to go after a zoning variance.

352
00:28:24,298 --> 00:28:24,598
[SPEAKER_08]: OK.

353
00:28:25,619 --> 00:28:28,842
[SPEAKER_04]: Because they were able to max out the roof yard.

354
00:28:29,843 --> 00:28:38,911
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, I had thought that I had mistakenly thought that under this scheme, they were going to have to go for a variance.

355
00:28:39,934 --> 00:28:43,350
[SPEAKER_03]: But she corrected me on that, the owner corrected me on that.

356
00:28:45,098 --> 00:28:46,558
[SPEAKER_03]: They maintain they won't have to go for a variance.

357
00:28:46,759 --> 00:28:50,480
[SPEAKER_03]: So I thought since they were going for a variance anyway, I asked them to push it up further.

358
00:28:50,540 --> 00:28:54,581
[SPEAKER_03]: But since they're not, I don't feel like I don't need to have that extra.

359
00:28:55,101 --> 00:28:57,282
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't want to put them through that in other words.

360
00:28:57,302 --> 00:29:03,724
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, I think the only change that I would make is the corner boards, making sure that those are there.

361
00:29:04,104 --> 00:29:14,507
[SPEAKER_04]: And then on the left side proposal, and it'll mimic it on the other side, it needs Eve returns, just little ones, especially if you're going to have the corner boards.

362
00:29:15,708 --> 00:29:19,370
[SPEAKER_04]: There, yeah.

363
00:29:20,711 --> 00:29:21,051
[SPEAKER_08]: Okay.

364
00:29:24,934 --> 00:29:33,260
[SPEAKER_04]: Then I do think that the front door should look like two doors to the best of the ability.

365
00:29:33,300 --> 00:29:36,983
[SPEAKER_04]: Even if that means making it wider, so be it.

366
00:29:37,363 --> 00:29:38,984
[SPEAKER_03]: To me, this looks like two doors.

367
00:29:39,605 --> 00:29:40,225
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, it's close.

368
00:29:40,586 --> 00:29:42,207
[SPEAKER_03]: Even though it's a single door,

369
00:29:43,111 --> 00:30:02,621
[SPEAKER_03]: yeah, and I know that they make doors like that, but again, you know, there are, I know, I know there are some availability issues out there, but that was one of my comments as well as I thought that I didn't really like the proportions of the doors.

370
00:30:02,741 --> 00:30:05,202
[SPEAKER_03]: I, anyway.

371
00:30:07,721 --> 00:30:09,803
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, I think these need much more detail.

372
00:30:09,903 --> 00:30:12,626
[SPEAKER_01]: And I'd like to see pictures of the doors.

373
00:30:12,646 --> 00:30:18,071
[SPEAKER_01]: If there's a supply issue, then, you know, okay, we're give give us a few options.

374
00:30:18,151 --> 00:30:22,034
[SPEAKER_01]: And let us say like, yes, we're okay with any of all of these, whatever you can procure.

375
00:30:22,054 --> 00:30:32,184
[SPEAKER_01]: I think there just needs to be more discussion around what it's actually going to look like these seem still very, I don't know, unfinished to me.

376
00:30:38,625 --> 00:30:42,221
[SPEAKER_01]: Any, I'm curious if Kit or Ed or Jess.

377
00:30:43,280 --> 00:30:44,761
[SPEAKER_01]: hasn't have any comments here.

378
00:30:45,782 --> 00:30:47,143
[SPEAKER_02]: I agree with you, Jen.

379
00:30:47,223 --> 00:31:03,856
